# Python dependencies for ansible-role-vault
# Source file for pip-compile. DO NOT edit requirements.txt directly.
#
# REGENERATE REPRODUCIBLY. The lock is a generated artifact and must be produced
# on the platform CI installs it on, or the hash set drifts: --generate-hashes
# enumerates the wheels the resolver can SEE, which depends on OS, architecture
# and Python version. Regenerating on macOS rewrote ~184 lines for no semantic
# reason. CI is ubuntu-latest x86_64 with Python 3.11, so:
#
#   docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64 -v "$PWD:/w" -w /w python:3.11-slim \
#     sh -c 'pip install -q pip-tools==7.6.1 && \
#            pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in'
#
# PIN THE GENERATOR. An unpinned `pip install pip-tools` makes the output depend
# on whichever release is current at regeneration time; the committed lock was
# produced by 7.6.1. Running that exact command twice yields BYTE-IDENTICAL
# output, which is what makes the artifact reproducible from its own procedure.
#
# Run it against the EXISTING requirements.txt, never a fresh path. pip-compile
# honours the pins already in its output file, so an unrelated transitive is not
# silently upgraded -- a fresh-path run pulled urllib3 2.8.0, which was ONE DAY
# OLD and inside the 7-day cooldown floor .github/dependabot.yml sets precisely
# to catch a malicious or yanked upstream release.
#
# THE `--no-index` IN THE GENERATED HEADER IS A pip-tools RENDERING BUG, not a
# flag anyone passed and not one that reached pip. Do not "fix" the documented
# command to match it, and do not pass it: the lock would then be resolved from
# whatever happens to be in the local cache.
#
#   Mechanism (piptools/utils.py get_compile_command, 7.6.1): the header builder
#   skips an option when `option.default == value`. For --no-index click reports
#   default `Sentinel.UNSET`, so UNSET == False is False and the guard never
#   fires; the option has no secondary `--index` opt, so the emitter falls to
#   `arg = option_long_name` and prints the flag regardless of its False value.
#
#   Evidence it was never in effect: in a fresh container with an empty pip cache
#   and `--network none`, pip-compile FAILS with
#   "DistributionNotFound: No matching distribution found for hvac>=2.0.0".
#   Resolution requires the index; with --no-index genuinely active it could not
#   have succeeded with the network up either.
#
# Classification: UNCLASSIFIED

# HashiCorp Vault API client - required by community.hashi_vault collection
# https://pypi.org/project/hvac/
# Supports Vault v1.4.7+, Python 3.8+
hvac>=2.0.0

# Address classification used by ansible.utils.ipaddr in tasks/preflight/dns.yml.
# The collection declares netaddr>=0.10.1; it is a CONTROLLER-side requirement.
netaddr>=0.10.1
